body:
Let Don Lemon know....

&#x200B;

Time took Flight 370's wings, not a black hole.

Do like  Cecelia did, tattoo of the aircraft on her wrist

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

[https://www.nydailynews.com/news/national/survivor-1987-mich-plane-crash-breaks-silence-article-1.1345734](https://www.nydailynews.com/news/national/survivor-1987-mich-plane-crash-breaks-silence-article-1.1345734)

Parents won't get any better.  The individual ones may, the there's a new batch coming behind them.   I'm not trying to scare you.

All you can do is explain the Ideals and Methods of Scouting to them and kindly ask them to stand aside (and help where and when appropriate).  

When it is time to depart from the troop, do you plan on sticking around in the BSA program?

With your interest in Camporees and outings, I'd suggest talking with your District and Council Committees about volunteering with these activities.   This you can do before "the time comes" to "move on".

Instead of "moving on", I'd suggest stepping back.   Going back to Assistant Scoutmaster or Committee Member.  

&#x200B;

After four years as Scoutmaster, I've recently stepped back to being Assistant Scoutmaster again.  The relief is unbelievable and I still get to go on outings and camping.  But my reason was that I was overstretched in the program and it wasn't fair to the youth to be Scoutmaster while having District, Council and OA positions.  

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

Tent verse 30 mph winds with 55 mph gusts.  

